er and Shmuel.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 76b:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_76b.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ketubot 21a:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_21a.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Ketubot 60a:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_60a.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3231:1:link-017","he":[644,731],"en":[1030,1149],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_44a.6"},"reference":"Chullin 44a:6","assessment":"Hullin expressly has Rav and is preserved separately from the Ketubbot passages.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 44a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_44a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3231:1:link-018","he":[733,796],"en":[1238,1251],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_32a.9"},"reference":"Kiddushin 32a:9","assessment":"Kiddushin directly supplies the family scene and Rav Yehudah’s intervention.","evidence":[{"reference":"Kiddushin 32a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_32a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3231:1:link-019","he":[798,864],"en":[1254,1346],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_138b.5"},"reference":"Shabbat 138b:5","assessment":"The attribution direction is Rami to Rav Huna for teachings of Rav.","evidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 138b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_138b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3231:1:link-020","he":[866,921],"en":[1347,1422],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_102a.13"},"reference":"Eruvin 102a:13","assessment":"The attribution direction is Rami to Rav Amram for the teaching of Rav Assi.","evidence":[{"reference":"Eruvin 102a:13","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_102a.13"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3231:1:link-021","he":[923,1014],"en":[1423,1466],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Taanit_2.14.3"},"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Taanit 2:14:3","assessment":"The checked Yerushalmi Taanit gives a chain through Rabbi Ba via Rabbi Immi bar Yehezkel, alongside a separate transmission via Rabbi Zeora. Yerushalmi Eruvin has R. Ba, Ami bar Yehezkel, and Rav in compressed succession. Identity with the Babylonian Rami remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Taanit 2:14:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Taanit_2.14.3"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Eruvin 5:1:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Eruvin_5.1.12"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]},{"id":"3231:1:link-022","he":[923,1014],"en":[1566,1603],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Eruvin_5.1.12"},"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Eruvin 5:1:12","assessment":"The checked Yerushalmi Taanit gives a chain through Rabbi Ba via Rabbi Immi bar Yehezkel, alongside a separate transmission via Rabbi Zeora. Yerushalmi Eruvin has R. Ba, Ami bar Yehezkel, and Rav in compressed succession. Identity with the Babylonian Rami remains open.","evidence":[{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Eruvin 5:1:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Eruvin_5.1.12"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Taanit 2:14:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Taanit_2.14.3"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]},{"id":"3231:1:link-023","he":[1016,1129],"en":[1651,1837],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_111b.22"},"reference":"Ketubot 111b:22","assessment":"Ketubbot explicitly attests speaker and episode. It locates the goats under the fig trees and describes the milk and honey mingling.","evidence":[{"reference":"Ketubot 111b:22","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Ketubot_111b.22"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,11,13,16,17,18,19,20,22],"holds":[{"raw":"רמי בר רב מאי עד כו' ל\"ת","reason":"The two occurrences of the siglum remain visible. The gloss does not itself resolve the divergent patronymics.","evidence":[{"reference":"Taanit 9a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Taanit_9a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Shabbat 32b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_32b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Makkot 23b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Makkot_23b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"יחזקאל ל\"ח.","reason":"Preserve the literal siglum. The immediate gloss and parallel settle the name comparison but not the siglum’s expansion.","evidence":[{"reference":"Zevachim 62b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Zevachim_62b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"raw":"צ\"ע איזה יכשר ל\"ת","reason":"Preserve the gloss’s own uncertainty and the textual contradiction.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 110a:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_110a.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Menachot 29b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Menachot_29b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The three witnesses of the until-sufficiency teaching are recorded separately. Zevahim includes both patronymics, and the Tamrei and Dekulei relationship remains disputed. Ketubbot’s Shmuel tradition and Hullin’s Rav tradition are distinct. The Yerushalmi attributions do not settle the identity of Ammi and Rami.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Shabbat 32b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Shabbat_32b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Kiddushin 32a:9","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_32a.9"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Taanit 2:14:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Taanit_2.14.3"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Eruvin 5:1:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Eruvin_5.1.12"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud, edition by Heinrich W. Guggenheimer. Berlin, De Gruyter, 1999-2015"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
